---
description: Use Cursor background agents as sidecar workers, not as the coordinator
alwaysApply: true
---

When background agents are available, use them for parallel sidecar tasks such as:

- researching an unfamiliar subsystem
- checking test failures
- verifying a risky migration path
- preparing a second opinion on a change

Guidelines:

- Keep the main chat as the coordinator that synthesizes results.
- Delegate bounded tasks with clear outputs.
- Do not launch multiple agents that edit the same files at the same time.
- Prefer background agents for read-heavy or isolated tasks, not for vague open-ended delegation.
